    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** stands as the undisputed anchor of the Austin Waves, posting an elite 76.75 score. Facing Liberatore (4.28 xERA), **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable platoon advantage and a premium batting order position, making him a lock for production. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** (67.14) remains a primary play despite facing a formidable arm in Wheeler; his immense park factor advantage and the sheer volume of his offensive contributions keep him well above the start threshold, even with the suppressed stolen base expectancy caused by an elite opposing battery. **Jackson Merrill** (63.55) and **Andy Pages** (62.47) also secure strong spots in the lineup, with **Andy Pages** providing sneaky upside due to his ability to exploit the slow delivery of Jake Bennett to boost our stolen base totals, our highest-priority category.\n\nThe toughest decision of the day involved the decision to bench **Wade Meckler** (35.18). Despite his speed profile, the matchup against Misiorowski and his 2.07 xERA created a prohibitive floor issue. Even with a platoon advantage, **Wade Meckler** fell well below our 40.0 efficiency threshold, as the risk of a sub-optimal performance outweighed the potential for a lone stolen base. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Kyle Tucker** (62.70) and **Andy Pages** (62.47); while both are projected as strong starts, the \"Lineup Pending\" status necessitates a final check to ensure their implied batting order holds, as any move to the bottom of the order could significantly dampen their daily efficiency. Caution is advised with **Luis Robert Jr.** (51.38), who is facing a difficult platoon scenario against Alcantara, though his raw talent keeps him in the lineup over bench options like **Denzer Guzman**.",
